{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And you shall see.</b> By the holy spirit that is upon you." "<b>Able men.</b> Wealthy men, who have no need to flatter or show favoritism (there)." "<b>Men of truth.</b> These are men of reliability, who are worthy to be trusted in their words — for through this their words will be heeded." "<b>Haters of gain.</b> Who hate their own money in a lawsuit — as that which we say: any judge from whom money is taken in judgment is not a judge (Bava Batra 58)." "<b>Chiefs of thousands.</b> These were six hundred chiefs over six hundred thousand." "<b>Chiefs of thousands.</b> There were six thousand." "<b>Chiefs of fifties.</b> Twelve thousand." "<b>Chiefs of tens.</b> Sixty thousand."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:53:03.493336520Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}